{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:01:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug about improper session management in the auto-tuning process has been resolved. You can check the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/AutoTuneForce/pull/47.", "utterranceID": "20261217-0-0a93f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-0-0a93f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:03:00", "text": "Great news, @eid_6a0f49ba! Can you explain what the root cause was?", "utterranceID": "20261217-1-6e78d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-1-6e78d"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:06:00", "text": "Sure, Ian. The root cause was a failure to implement robust session management practices. Specifically, session tokens used during the auto-tuning process weren't being invalidated in a timely manner. This left them vulnerable to hijacking, allowing attackers to alter model parameters.", "utterranceID": "20261217-2-7637c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-2-7637c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:07:00", "text": "Got it. How did you manage to fix it?", "utterranceID": "20261217-3-4d32c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-3-4d32c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:10:00", "text": "We addressed the issue by implementing a more secure session management protocol. Now, session tokens are automatically invalidated after each tuning session. Additionally, we've added checks to ensure tokens are only valid for a single use, reducing the risk of them being reused maliciously.", "utterranceID": "20261217-4-44acb"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-4-44acb"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:13:00", "text": "That sounds like a solid fix, George. Thanks for taking care of this so quickly!", "utterranceID": "20261217-5-276aa"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-5-276aa"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-18T04:14:00", "text": "No problem, @eid_35e32fec. Let me know if you need any more details or if there's anything else I can help with.", "utterranceID": "20261217-6-4bf32"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261217-6-4bf32"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T12:59:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Memory Leak in Parameter Storage' has been resolved. 🎉", "utterranceID": "20261226-0-994f5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-0-994f5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T13:03:00", "text": "The issue was due to improper memory management in the parameter storage module, which caused a gradual memory leak. This led to the optimization engine losing track of parameter updates over time.", "utterranceID": "20261226-1-6545e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-1-6545e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6a0f49ba", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T13:07:00", "text": "I've submitted a fix that ensures proper deallocation of memory after each parameter update cycle. This prevents memory exhaustion and maintains the integrity of parameter history. You can check the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/AutoTuneForce/pull/48", "utterranceID": "20261226-2-5e8ee"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-2-5e8ee"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce", "channelID": "ch-force-35b4b2"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_35e32fec", "timestamp": "2026-12-26T13:11:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_6a0f49ba! Thanks for addressing this so quickly. I'll review the PR shortly.", "utterranceID": "20261226-3-08037"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261226-3-08037"}
