{"transcript": "Attendees\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\nTranscript\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's go over the completed PRs. Charlie, can you start with the user authentication endpoints?\nCharlie Martinez: Sure, Julia. The user authentication endpoints are up and running. We've implemented both login and registration functionalities, and everything's been tested thoroughly. No issues reported so far.\nBob Miller: Great work, Charlie. This is crucial for securing our API. How about the JWT token verification middleware?\nDavid Miller: I can take that. The middleware for JWT token verification is also complete. It’s working as expected, ensuring only requests with valid tokens can access protected routes.\nHannah Brown: Fantastic. These are significant steps forward for our security. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks. First up, the hardware compatibility checks. Julia Smith, can you update us on the status?\nJulia Smith: Sure, Hannah. I submitted a PR for updating the device layer to enhance protocol handling, but it needs some revisions. Fiona, you'll be taking over this, right?\nFiona Taylor: Yes, Julia. I'll work on the new PR and make sure to address the feedback. I'll submit it by the end of the week.\nJulia Martinez: Great, Fiona. Please keep us posted on your progress. Next, we have the development of the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, you're up for this task, correct?\nAlice Garcia: That's right, Julia. I'll be working on creating the data retrieval endpoints. I'll start on this today and aim to have a draft by mid-week.\nBob Miller: Perfect, Alice. This will be key for enabling real-time insights. Lastly, we have the implementation of JWT authentication for security. Charlie Miller, you're handling this one?\nCharlie Miller: Yes, Bob. I'll update the access control policies to integrate with the new JWT authentication system. I'll ensure that user permissions are checked based on the JWT claims.\nDavid Miller: Sounds good, Charlie. Do you have an estimated timeline for this?\nCharlie Miller: I plan to have it ready for review by the end of next week.\nHannah Brown: Alright, team. Let's make sure we stay on track with these tasks. If anyone needs help or runs into issues, don't hesitate to reach out. Thanks, everyone, for your hard work.\nJulia Martinez: Yes, thank you all. Let's keep the momentum going. Meeting adjourned.", "date": "2026-11-07T00:40:00", "document_type": "product-planning", "participants": ["eid_91523bad", "eid_b6a30126", "eid_caa2e58d", "eid_2d8eff4d", "eid_a253c65a", "eid_4b38019b", "eid_2347b567", "eid_bac7c6c4", "eid_edf6a3fc", "eid_4df3bcc2", "eid_54905dcb", "eid_4555ba9c", "eid_3e076e53", "eid_5058fefc", "eid_a0fe567d"], "id": "product_dev_EdgeForce_6"}

{"transcript": "Attendees\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\nTranscript\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, welcome to our first sprint review for the Einstein Edge AI project. Let's dive into the status of our tasks and PRs. Since this is our first meeting, we don't have any completed PRs to discuss, so we'll focus on our pending tasks.\nBob Miller: Sounds good, Julia. Let's start with the hardware compatibility checks. Julia Smith, you're assigned to this task, right?\nJulia Smith: Yes, that's correct. I'm working on the PR titled 'Add Support for New Sensor Protocols'. The goal is to update the device layer to recognize and process data from new sensor types.\nHannah Brown: Julia, do you foresee any challenges with implementing support for these new protocols?\nJulia Smith: Not at the moment, but I'll keep an eye on any compatibility issues that might arise during testing.\nJulia Martinez: Great. Let's move on to the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, you're handling this one, correct?\nAlice Garcia: Yes, I'm on it. The PR is titled 'Initialize RESTful API Framework'. I'll be setting up the foundational structure and ensuring we have all the necessary libraries and configurations in place.\nCharlie Martinez: Alice, do you need any additional resources or support to get started?\nAlice Garcia: Not at the moment, Charlie. I have everything I need to kick things off. I'll reach out if anything comes up.\nJulia Martinez: Perfect. Lastly, we have the JWT authentication task. Charlie Miller, you're assigned to this, right?\nCharlie Miller: Yes, that's me. The PR is 'Implement JWT Token Generation and Validation'. I'll be working on creating a utility module for handling JWT operations.\nDavid Miller: Charlie, make sure to coordinate with the API team to ensure seamless integration.\nCharlie Miller: Got it, David. I'll make sure to sync up with Alice and the rest of the API team.\nJulia Martinez: Alright, team. Let's make sure we keep communication open and address any blockers as they come up. Does anyone have any questions or need further clarification on their tasks?\nFiona Taylor: No questions from me. Everything seems clear.\nAlice Miller: Same here. I'm good to go.\nJulia Martinez: Great. Let's aim to have significant progress by our next meeting. Thanks, everyone!", "date": "2026-09-25T04:45:00", "document_type": "product-planning", "participants": ["eid_91523bad", "eid_b6a30126", "eid_caa2e58d", "eid_2d8eff4d", "eid_a253c65a", "eid_4b38019b", "eid_2347b567", "eid_bac7c6c4", "eid_edf6a3fc", "eid_4df3bcc2", "eid_54905dcb", "eid_4555ba9c", "eid_3e076e53", "eid_5058fefc", "eid_a0fe567d"], "id": "product_dev_EF_AIX_2"}

