{"transcript": "Attendees\nGeorge Garcia, Fiona Miller, Fiona Brown, Fiona Davis, Hannah Smith, Bob Brown, David Miller, George Smith, Fiona Miller, Emma Brown, Hannah Brown, Emma Taylor, Alice Taylor, Hannah Smith, Hannah Garcia, Emma Jones, David Williams, George Jones, David Miller, David Martinez, Emma Smith, Ian Garcia, Hannah Williams, Bob Garcia, Julia Davis, David Jones, Hannah Johnson, Ian Davis, Fiona Davis, Hannah Garcia, Alice Smith, George Brown, Hannah Garcia, Emma Williams, George Johnson, Alice Jones, David Taylor, Bob Davis, David Miller, David Smith, Julia Miller, Hannah Miller, Fiona Taylor, Julia Davis, Bob Martinez, Fiona Davis, Julia Miller\nTranscript\nGeorge Garcia: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's go over the completed PRs. Fiona Miller, could you start with the GraphQL API optimization?\nFiona Miller: Sure, George. The 'Optimize GraphQL API for Performance' PR has been successfully merged. We've implemented several optimizations that significantly reduce load times and improve data retrieval efficiency. The feedback from the initial tests has been positive.\nGeorge Garcia: Great work, Fiona. This should really enhance the user experience. Next, Bob Brown, could you update us on the network quality monitoring integration?\nBob Brown: Absolutely. The 'Integrate Network Quality Monitoring' PR is complete. We've added tools that provide real-time feedback on connection quality. This should help users troubleshoot network issues more effectively during collaboration sessions.\nGeorge Garcia: Excellent. This feature will be a game-changer for our users. Lastly, Fiona Brown, can you tell us about the API client libraries?\nFiona Brown: Yes, the 'Develop API Client Libraries for Popular Languages' PR is done. We've created libraries for Python, Java, and JavaScript, making it easier for developers to integrate CollaborateForce into their applications.\nGeorge Garcia: Fantastic. This will definitely broaden our reach. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks. Emma Jones, you're up for the API design with GraphQL. Can you update us on the documentation task?\nEmma Jones: Sure thing, George. The task is to add comprehensive documentation for the GraphQL API. This includes usage examples, schema details, and integration guidelines. I'll be handling the implementation.\nGeorge Garcia: Great, Emma. Just to confirm, you'll be taking care of the 'Add Documentation for GraphQL API Usage' PR?\nEmma Jones: Yes, I confirm. I'll take care of this implementation.\nGeorge Garcia: Perfect. Does anyone have any questions or need further clarification on any of the tasks?\nHannah Smith: I just wanted to clarify the timeline for the documentation task. Emma, do you have an estimated completion date?\nEmma Jones: I'm aiming to have it completed by the end of next week. I'll keep everyone updated on my progress.\nGeorge Garcia: Sounds good. If there are no more questions, let's wrap up. Thanks, everyone, for your hard work and dedication. Let's keep up the momentum!", "date": "2026-11-16T21:45:00", "document_type": "product-planning", "participants": ["eid_0c373165", "eid_1330d187", "eid_ab6f41bc", "eid_131494b8", "eid_16935c12", "eid_d3a4fc8f", "eid_2d14387c", "eid_9f1ff493", "eid_54b986cf", "eid_4988ee2a", "eid_0e2e8d07", "eid_3516c527", "eid_ec5cb5c2", "eid_1e7c8290", "eid_a7dd9c52", "eid_446bc3ee", "eid_a8040636", "eid_13df35ed", "eid_76d9cb07", "eid_df7ae03e", "eid_b3fcc490", "eid_0aa9f1f7", "eid_a88ee967", "eid_abbf3651", "eid_737797e3", "eid_ec70ac57", "eid_619c8be2", "eid_7dfbbca2", "eid_7fba1318", "eid_9e9883de", "eid_67036b20", "eid_f0c7a505", "eid_63ea0ec4", "eid_2594f98a", "eid_69130545", "eid_8986ddc3", "eid_70223d0a", "eid_67416adf", "eid_987771ee", "eid_c2a92a40", "eid_4d18a84c", "eid_a1fab288", "eid_8cbee5b3", "eid_c42e5095", "eid_86f94a48", "eid_01e37306", "eid_724e1180"], "id": "product_dev_CollaborateForce_9"}

