lor: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation. I'll ensure the API is robust and efficient.\nJulia Taylor: Perfect. Moving on to 'Improving integration with third-party applications'. David, you're assigned to 'Update API Documentation for Third-Party Integration'.\nDavid Garcia: Understood, I'll make sure the documentation is comprehensive and user-friendly.\nJulia Taylor: Lastly, 'Enhancing user interface'. Hannah, your PR needs additional revisions, and George, you'll work on a new PR for this.\nHannah Brown: I'll make the necessary revisions and ensure the filter options are more intuitive.\nGeorge Johnson: And I'll start fresh on the new PR to enhance usability. I'll coordinate with Hannah to ensure consistency.\nJulia Taylor: Excellent. Let's aim to have these tasks completed by the end of the sprint. Any questions or concerns before we wrap up?\nFiona Davis: Just a quick note, let's ensure we have regular check-ins to track progress and address any blockers.\nJulia Taylor: Absolutely, Fiona. We'll schedule those. Thanks, everyone, for your hard work and dedication. Let's make this sprint a success!", "date": "2026-12-02T13:12:00", "document_type": "product-planning", "participants": ["eid_d0b6cb92", "eid_439a052b", "eid_6d14c4ec", "eid_887367ca", "eid_5b61c55e", "eid_efc9418c", "eid_aa99608e", "eid_9b8bc088", "eid_e5715d9e", "eid_160fca3c", "eid_13786f09", "eid_7db4431d", "eid_3fa288cf", "eid_990f697c", "eid_b7f0726e", "eid_0aa7db32", "eid_7bd14403", "eid_e7622cfb", "eid_51f0b41f", "eid_070b6e41", "eid_12c203a5", "eid_681e9def", "eid_b20b58ad", "eid_4eec2a5a"], "id": "product_dev_SearchForce_5"}

