Attendees
Julia Taylor, Alice Smith, David Williams, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Fiona Davis, Julia Martinez, David Taylor, Emma Johnson, David Garcia, Alice Taylor, David Jones, Hannah Brown, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Bob Jones, Charlie Jones, Fiona Taylor, Hannah Brown, Alice Miller, George Johnson, Bob Miller, Julia Jones, Alice Jones
Transcript
David Taylor: Team, let’s get started. Today our focus is on finalizing the next set of features for Salesforce AI Search. We need to ensure these align with our product goals and technical specifications. Let's dive into the precise feature discussion first.
George Davis: Absolutely, David. The first feature we need to discuss is enhancing our natural language processing capabilities. This is crucial for improving user query understanding and delivering more accurate search results.
David Williams: For this, we should consider expanding our training data to include more complex query patterns. We also need to refine our NLU models. Emma, could you take the lead on this?
Emma Johnson: Sure, David. I'll start by reviewing our current datasets and identify gaps. We might need to integrate additional data sources to improve model accuracy.
Alice Smith: Great. The second feature is the implementation of context awareness algorithms. This will help us retain context across user interactions, making search results more relevant.
Alice Taylor: I suggest we use a session-based approach to maintain context. We can store session data temporarily and use it to refine search results. I'll draft a proposal for the data structures and APIs needed.
Charlie Miller: Sounds good, Alice. The third feature is improving our integration with third-party applications. We need to ensure our APIs are robust and well-documented.
David Garcia: For this, we should enhance our error handling mechanisms and ensure API compatibility. I'll work on updating the API documentation and testing integration scenarios.
Fiona Davis: The fourth feature is enhancing our user interface. We need to incorporate more user feedback and improve the flexibility of search parameter configurations.
Hannah Brown: I can take this on. I'll gather recent user feedback and work with the design team to implement necessary UI changes. We should also consider A/B testing to validate improvements.

