{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_b6268ef7", "timestamp": "2026-11-05T06:33:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Unresponsive UI Elements During Data Drill-Down' has been resolved. You can check the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/FlowForce/pull/45.", "utterranceID": "20261105-0-5aa6a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261105-0-5aa6a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_b6268ef7", "timestamp": "2026-11-05T06:36:00", "text": "The root cause was identified as inefficient event handling in the UI layer. It was struggling to manage multiple user interactions during intensive data operations, which led to the unresponsiveness.", "utterranceID": "20261105-1-fa047"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261105-1-fa047"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_b6268ef7", "timestamp": "2026-11-05T06:41:00", "text": "To fix this, I optimized the event handling by implementing a debounce mechanism. This ensures that the UI processes events at a manageable rate, preventing overload during data drill-down operations.", "utterranceID": "20261105-2-16bb1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261105-2-16bb1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-05T06:42:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_b6268ef7! That should make a big difference for users who need to analyze data in detail.", "utterranceID": "20261105-3-1e901"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261105-3-1e901"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d098d618", "timestamp": "2026-11-05T06:47:00", "text": "Thanks, Charlie! I'll make sure to test this thoroughly in the next QA cycle. @eid_b6268ef7, did you also update the documentation to reflect these changes?", "utterranceID": "20261105-4-25777"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261105-4-25777"}
