{"title": "Enhance API Authentication with Modern Security Protocols", "summary": "### Summary of the Issue\nThe API responsible for managing AI models on devices was found to have weak authentication mechanisms, making it vulnerable to unauthorized access through brute force attacks and credential stuffing.\n\n### Changes Made\n- Implemented OAuth 2.0 for secure authentication.\n- Added rate limiting to prevent brute force attacks.\n- Integrated multi-factor authentication (MFA) for an additional layer of security.\n- Updated documentation to reflect the new authentication process.\n\n### Testing\n- Conducted unit tests to ensure the new authentication flow works as expected.\n- Performed integration tests to verify compatibility with existing systems.\n- Simulated attack scenarios to confirm the robustness of the new security measures.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/EdgeForce/pull/37", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "True", "number": "37", "state": "closed", "user": {"login": "eid_2347b567"}, "created_at": "2027-01-23T23:50:00", "reviews": [{"state": "APPROVED", "user": {"login": "eid_91523bad"}, "comment": "The changes look great! The implementation of OAuth 2.0 and additional security measures significantly enhance the API's authentication process. All tests have passed, and the documentation is clear. Approved for merge.", "submitted_at": "2027-01-23T23:04:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_EdgeForce_pull_37"}

