{"transcript": "Attendees\nGeorge Garcia, Fiona Miller, Fiona Brown, Fiona Davis, Hannah Smith, Bob Brown, David Miller, George Smith, Fiona Miller, Emma Brown, Hannah Brown, Emma Taylor, Alice Taylor, Hannah Smith, Hannah Garcia, Emma Jones, David Williams, George Jones, David Miller, David Martinez, Emma Smith, Ian Garcia, Hannah Williams, Bob Garcia, Julia Davis, David Jones, Hannah Johnson, Ian Davis, Fiona Davis, Hannah Garcia, Alice Smith, George Brown, Hannah Garcia, Emma Williams, George Johnson, Alice Jones, David Taylor, Bob Davis, David Miller, David Smith, Julia Miller, Hannah Miller, Fiona Taylor, Julia Davis, Bob Martinez, Fiona Davis, Julia Miller\nTranscript\nGeorge Garcia: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. We'll start by discussing the completed PRs. First up, the Correction Capture System for AI Suggestions. Great work on that, everyone.\nDavid Miller: Yes, capturing user corrections is crucial for refining our AI model. This will definitely enhance the accuracy of our suggestions.\nAlice Taylor: Absolutely. Moving on, the GraphQL Schema for Data Points and Visualizations is now defined. This sets a solid foundation for our API work.\nEmma Jones: I agree. The schema will streamline our data access and manipulation processes.\nGeorge Garcia: Next, the Key Management System for Encryption Protocols is in place. This is a big step forward for our security measures.\nEmma Brown: Yes, ensuring secure key management is essential for our encryption protocols.\nGeorge Garcia: And finally, the Keyboard Navigation for UI Components and Advanced Data Visualization API Endpoints are both completed. Great job on enhancing accessibility and expanding our API capabilities.\nFiona Davis: Thanks, George. The keyboard navigation should really improve user experience.\nGeorge Garcia: Alright, let's move on to the pending tasks. First, the AI engine feedback loop. Hannah Garcia, you're up for integrating the feedback data into the AI model training pipeline.\nHannah Garcia: Got it, I’ll handle this. I'll ensure the feedback loop is robust and improves our model's learning.\nGeorge Garcia: Great. Next, API design with GraphQL. Emma Jones, you'll be implementing the resolvers for GraphQL queries and mutations.\nEmma Jones: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation. I'll make sure the data is fetched and manipulated correctly.\nGeorge Garcia: Perfect. Now, WebRTC optimization for collaboration tools. George Jones, your PR needs some revisions. Alice Jones, you'll be working on a new PR for bandwidth estimation and adaptation.\nGeorge Jones: Understood, I'll address the feedback and make the necessary revisions.\nAlice Jones: I'll take on the new PR. I'll focus on optimizing the bandwidth estimation and adaptation.\nGeorge Garcia: Thanks, Alice. Next, encryption protocols for communication features. Emma Brown, you'll be developing end-to-end encryption for group discussions.\nEmma Brown: I confirm, I’ll take care of this. Ensuring secure communication is a top priority.\nGeorge Garcia: Great. For UI components, David Taylor, you'll be creating customizable dashboards for different user roles.\nDavid Taylor: Got it, I’ll handle this. I'll focus on making the dashboards flexible and user-friendly.\nGeorge Garcia: Lastly, expanding API support. David Miller, you'll be enhancing the API with AI-powered suggestions.\nDavid Miller: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation. I'll ensure the suggestions are relevant and enhance collaboration.\nGeorge Garcia: Excellent. Thanks, everyone. Let's keep up the great work and make sure to reach out if you need any assistance. Meeting adjourned.", "date": "2026-09-10T00:25:00", "document_type": "product-planning", "participants": ["eid_0c373165", "eid_1330d187", "eid_ab6f41bc", "eid_131494b8", "eid_16935c12", "eid_d3a4fc8f", "eid_2d14387c", "eid_9f1ff493", "eid_54b986cf", "eid_4988ee2a", "eid_0e2e8d07", "eid_3516c527", "eid_ec5cb5c2", "eid_1e7c8290", "eid_a7dd9c52", "eid_446bc3ee", "eid_a8040636", "eid_13df35ed", "eid_76d9cb07", "eid_df7ae03e", "eid_b3fcc490", "eid_0aa9f1f7", "eid_a88ee967", "eid_abbf3651", "eid_737797e3", "eid_ec70ac57", "eid_619c8be2", "eid_7dfbbca2", "eid_7fba1318", "eid_9e9883de", "eid_67036b20", "eid_f0c7a505", "eid_63ea0ec4", "eid_2594f98a", "eid_69130545", "eid_8986ddc3", "eid_70223d0a", "eid_67416adf", "eid_987771ee", "eid_c2a92a40", "eid_4d18a84c", "eid_a1fab288", "eid_8cbee5b3", "eid_c42e5095", "eid_86f94a48", "eid_01e37306", "eid_724e1180"], "id": "product_dev_CollaborateForce_5"}


